00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:14.340
required mitigation measures. On the AI front, SpaceX denied a Wall Street Journal report that it had

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:21.280
shown an AI handset prototype ahead of the June IPO. The statement clarifies that no such device

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:27.640
was presented to investors during pre-IPO discussions. Any future handset work would tie into

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:33.180
Starlink direct to cell capacity planning already underway. From an engineering standpoint,

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:40.100
the 1000th Merlin 1D acceptance test illustrates how reuse converts each flight into a data source

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:45.820
that narrows the gap between raw material cost and finished engine price. A new Merlin

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:51.600
starts as forging, machined parts, and turbo pump assemblies whose input metals and propellants

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:57.860
represent only a small fraction of final unit cost. Each recovered engine returns with measured

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:04.380
wear on seals, injectors, and turbines. Those measurements drive targeted material or geometry

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:10.360
changes that extend life without wholesale redesign. Over hundreds of flights, the cumulative

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:16.240
effect has raised the engine's demonstrated reliability while the per-flight amortization of the

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:22.340
original hardware continues to fall. The same inspection to improvement loop is now being applied

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:28.360
to Raptor, where the open question is how quickly flight data can compress the idiot index on the

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:39.660
larger, higher thrust engine. And a quick market note, SPC-X closed at $157.54, down 0.2%.

